# ASTR 102: Introduction to Stellar and Solar Systems

## 📖 Course Overview & Syllabus
This course covers basic concepts of astronomy related to our Solar System[span_0](start_span)[span_0](end_span). Topics include units of cosmic distances, astronomy in Islamic civilization, the electromagnetic spectrum and telescopes, characteristics of the solar system and Kepler's laws, the Moon-Earth-Sun system and related phenomena, terrestrial planets, Jovian planets, and the origins of asteroids and comets[span_1](start_span)[span_1](end_span).

## 📝 Basic Info
* **Academic Level:** Level 03 (Second Year)[span_2](start_span)[span_2](end_span)
* **Prerequisites:** MATH 101[span_3](start_span)[span_3](end_span)
* **Core Focus:** Astronomy and Planetary Science

